Prompt:

Theme: {automotive / travel / sport / urban / photography / etc.}
Brand / Event: {name}
Main word: {short bold keyword}
Person: {adult character, outfit, vibe}
Interactive object: {steering wheel / suitcase / barbell / phone / camera / etc.}
Action: {natural interaction}
Typography color: {acid lime / orange / vermilion / violet / cyan / etc.}
Environment: {car / terminal / gym / metro / street / etc.}
Aspect ratio: 9:16

Create a clean full-bleed editorial campaign poster with realistic photography, oversized colored typography, and strong connected forced perspective.

The foreground object must be the same object the person is naturally holding, operating, pulling, or using. Keep a clear physical connection:

body → arm → hand → object.

Use a 20–28mm wide-angle perspective. The object appears oversized only because it is extremely close to the camera. Keep the grip, anatomy, object structure, and perspective realistic.

Place one huge condensed sans-serif keyword behind the subject using the selected bold color. Let the person, arm, and foreground object naturally overlap the letters to create depth.

Use a continuous full-bleed environment from top to bottom. The street, floor, vehicle interior, terminal, gym, or architecture should extend all the way to the bottom edge.

Do not add a separate footer band. Place bottom text directly over the scene.

Keep supporting information minimal and meaningful: brand, date, location, category, short specs, or action phrases.

Keep the person clean, sharp, and realistic with even skin tone, subtle pores, soft directional light, and natural matte-to-satin skin. Keep the face, hands, and foreground object sufficiently clear.

Avoid duplicated or floating objects, disconnected limbs, incorrect grips, distorted anatomy, oily or blotchy skin, excessive decoration, meaningless filler text, complex UI, CGI skin, and bottom footer bands.

Final result: a bold full-bleed poster with strong color identity, realistic connected action, dramatic depth, and high visual impact.

Prompt:

SUBJECT: {adult subject + identity}
OUTFIT: {outfit}
SCENE: {night location}
EXPRESSION: {mood}
COLOR PALETTE: {colors}
ASPECT RATIO: {9:16}

Create a realistic ultra-close night fashion portrait with an “almost collision” POV.

The adult subject is genuinely walking toward the photographer while the photographer backs away. Capture a real mid-step moment, with natural shoulder rotation, walking inertia, and the body still moving forward. The subject is already so close that another half-step would require them to move aside.

Use an 18–22mm full-frame-equivalent wide-angle lens, about 30–45 cm from the nearest shoulder and upper torso. Keep the camera only slightly above eye level with a gentle 7–15° downward angle.

Aim the optical axis around the clavicle and sternum rather than the face. Let the upper torso sit near the center of the frame, with the face slightly higher and the waist, hips, and upper thighs receding naturally.

Add a subtle fisheye-like character: mild barrel distortion, gentle central bulging, and slight peripheral stretching. Keep it controlled and photographic — no extreme fisheye or GoPro distortion.

The near-collision feeling must come from torso-to-camera distance, not from reaching toward the lens. Keep both hands beside the body in natural walking motion.

Use strong direct flash to freeze the subject sharply against a darker night environment. Preserve realistic skin pores, natural texture, real hair strands, flyaways, believable fabric, and small motion traces in hair or clothing.

Use a different adult face for every new image while keeping the same camera language.

Tight head-to-upper-thigh framing, minimal empty space, slightly imperfect composition, strong physical proximity, and the feeling that the subject is one step away from bumping into the camera.

Avoid static poses, giant foreground hands, repeated faces, extreme top-down angles, extreme fisheye, distorted anatomy, plastic skin, oily highlights, CGI rendering, excessive neon, and studio lookbook styling.

